{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959539-privileges-for-all-covenants","id":959539,"title":"Privileges for all Covenants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-28T15:58:41-07:00","id":959539,"title":"Privileges for all Covenants","content":"I've just wondered if someone has made some homewbrew Covenant Advantages for those Covenants who were only mentioned (like the ones from the example Vampire settings or the Broken Covenants), or have updated those extra Covenants from 1e (like the ones from Danse Macabre or Ancient Mysteries). For now, I've only had ideas for the Tenth Choir and the Kataramenos (the first would be some sort of &quot;divine vision&quot; in the form of developing weird, angelic eyes over their body while the other would have an updated version of Veneficia. Still has to write either of those, however).<br /> <br /> So- which ideas did you had as gifts for the extra Covenants?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:55:11-07:00","id":960875,"title":"","content":"I wrote up something for the Brides of Dracula. I wanted to put a little more history to their story so when other Charters moved into Europe, being nomadic as the Brides were they discovered remnants of the Gallows Post and twisted their secrets and practices to their own ends. Expanding their influence against the other Covenants and giving them a little something all their own. Now what I'm including below is the first draft of merits I worked out for them. Still loose on the rules but since I have no PC's in my game playing them I'm taking my time tightening the crunch aspect of it.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawing a Line (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Brides of Dracula Status and Craft <b>\u2022\u2022 </b>or Occult <b>\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Effect: </b>Brides understand the importance of a place to rest after a long ride, but it\u2019s difficult when you have no real roots. Drawing a Line Merit provides them a temporary Haven and Safe Place equal to the dots in Brides of Dracula Status which may not be added to existing dots in those Merits. A Bride must take a Scene to prepare the place for it to be suitable for their needs.<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Draw a Line is not exclusive to the Merit holder. Any covenant member with a dot of status is allowed to use it as well whether the merit-holder wants them to or not. The same drawback under Haven is applied to it as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Patched In (\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Brides of Dracula Status<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Brides maintain an entourage around them of followers, friends and family, sometimes indistinguishable from one another. Divide dots equal to your Bride\u2019s status in the Herd, Staff, and Retainers Merits. You may distribute them as you like. These dots can be added to existing Merit dots, or added upon later. If she loses dots of Status, the dots granted by this Merit go away as well.<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>These advantages ride with the covenant. Should you lose your patch they may turn on you, or those too loyal are put down hard, but either way they are stripped away.<br /> <br /> <b>Bride\u2019s Vows</b><br /> The Bride\u2019s Vows Merits are their edge when it comes to contending with the other covenants. Learned from the Gallows Post but twisted to suit their own ends, it\u2019s what allows the Brides to flout the laws of the domains they are passing through or taking up as their new turf. The Vows ease the burdens a vampire faces when choosing to nomadically exist on a nightly basis.<br /> <br /> <b>Road-Wise (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Brides of Dracula Status <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> The President of a chapter knows the roads like their own blood. How it functions like the circulatory pulse linking all civilization together. The President and the club must begin their ride on a road at the beginning of the night, any road (even dirt roads), and over the course of a night right before dawn may reach any destination over any distance as long as there is a connecting physical route.<br /> The ride itself takes on a hypnotic quality. There is no breaking for a rest stop as time seems to move both in slow motion and rapid pace, at the end of which one Vitae is taken from each vampire and ghoul, humans are exhausted, hungry and sleepy, and all the vehicles gasoline tanks are near empty. The price the Road takes as payment, along with some pretty strange daydreams or nightmares about an angel of the road riding a world machine.<br /> <br /> <b>Fuck Your Rules (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Brides of Dracula Status <b>\u2022</b><br /> <b>Effect: </b>Blood Bonds, Carthian Laws, Invictus Oaths, various Disciplines like Dominate and Majesty, even Conditions caused by Predatory Aura, these are the tools used by Kindred elite to keep the sheep in line. A Bride subjected to any of these following methods has only one recourse, find a bolt hole to lay low or get the hell out of town.<br /> A Bride of Dracula under any of the influences mentioned above can circumvent the hold by returning to a designated Bride\u2019s Haven or by leaving the domain for a period of time equal to the effect in question. Should they leave the Haven or return to the domain prematurely, the effect resumes until the time has either elapsed or they again return to the Haven or exit the domain. The Kindred who applied the effect where applicable is unaware that the Bride has found a way around it<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Of course many Brides suffering under the hold of these effects might need assistance to actually apply this Merit (such as the case of a third stage Blood Bond). The other members of the covenant need to first be aware something is wrong with their covenant mate to help them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T05:35:48-07:00","id":960992,"title":"","content":"Very cool advantages. Question: Is it that the Brides discover their euro counterpart is the old gallows post or do they just plunder the old when they find it? If not, is it like the Invictus-Camarila connection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T22:48:32-07:00","id":961464,"title":"","content":"I had it in mind they found it, plundered it and distributed it Covenant wide. I was thinking though a Torpid Elder woke up, liked their cuts and joined along. Especially since according to Dark Era's towards then end Gallows Post was becoming a bit more political.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}